t we can rewrite the terms of the series as powers of $\\frac{e}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+\\frac{e}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{9}+⋯+\\frac{{e}^{n}}{{3}^{n}}+⋯ & =1+\\frac{{e}^{1}}{{3}^{1}}+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+⋯+\\frac{{e}^{n}}{{3}^{n}}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{1}+{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{2}+⋯+{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{n}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯+{x}^{n}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{e}{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1-\\frac{e}{3})} & =1+\\frac{e}{3}+{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{2}+{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{3}+⋯+{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{n}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{3}{3-e} & =1+\\frac{e}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{e}^{3}}{27}+⋯+\\frac{{e}^{n}}{{3}^{n}}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{3}{3-e}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348491 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348491 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348491 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "050753b8-7157-59d9-9cc5-ea5d0d3633ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348716 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e+1)-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348716 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348716 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1edb4e4c-d263-53d9-a119-691647dd55a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349266 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349266 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349266 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5942ff78-62e6-5b2f-a5b6-4f5f6bc2efd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349365 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e-1)+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349365 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349365 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64296992-5700-539e-a388-c0c77c90623d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350696 #edb/ref 1080 